WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.442
The next module moves from joins to subqueries.

00:00:03.442 --> 00:00:06.317
A join combines row sets directly.

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:12.242
A subquery allows one query to use the result of another query as part of its logic.

00:00:12.242 --> 00:00:19.562
You will see subqueries used for questions such as: which patients have an admission above the average length

00:00:19.562 --> 00:00:26.142
of stay, which customers have at least one large order, or which products have never appeared in a sales

00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:29.462
table. The join skills from this module still matter.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:36.757
When deciding between a join, a subquery, or a common table expression, continue asking about grain,

00:00:36.757 --> 00:00:37.782
cardinality, and clarity.

00:00:37.782 --> 00:00:45.052
Before moving on, make sure you can explain the difference between matching and preservation,

00:00:45.052 --> 00:00:49.817
and make sure you understand why several detail tables can multiply rows.

00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:54.127
Those two ideas will continue to appear in more advanced SQL.

00:00:54.127 --> 00:00:59.912
As SQL becomes more expressive, the goal is not to use the most advanced syntax.

00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:05.040
The goal is to write logic that is correct, understandable, and easy to validate.
